        <item>
            <title>0.15.8</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 10:25:48 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>169</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.8</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.2</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
<li>The other side of a call is no longer lost on slower Macs. On an 8 GB machine the system-audio tap can take several seconds to warm up; the watchdog was tearing it down and rebuilding every 1.5 s, which reset that warm-up and then falsely warned &quot;other side not recorded&quot; even though the tap recovered on its own moments later. It now gives a slow tap time to come up instead of fighting it, so the first seconds of the far end survive.</li>
<li>The transcription status now reads &quot;Loading the model…&quot; instead of &quot;Optimizing for your Mac&quot;, which wrongly implied a one-time setup was running again every session when the model was actually already installed.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
